  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $2.1B in FY2027 to date. The Department of Homeland Security made 3,019 awards with an average award size of $704K, and obligations fell 97.1% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show obligations of $20.8B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $23.6B in FY24, $28.3B in FY25, $73.3B in FY26, and $2.1B in FY27. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest NAICS category in FY2027 to date at $609M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $307M and All Other Travel Arrangement and Reservation Services at $279M. SOUTHWEST VALLEY CONSTRUCTORS CO is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date at $283M, followed by CSI AVIATION, INC at $278M and WHITING-TURNER CONTRACTING COMPANY, THE at $155M. The figures are contract obligations and the FY2027 totals are fiscal year to date, so the reported totals are partial for the current year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 spending compare to prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $2.1B in FY27 compared with $73.3B in FY26. Obligations were $20.8B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $23.6B in FY24, and $28.3B in FY25, showing a sharp decline in the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest buys and who wins them in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads NAICS categories at $609M, with Security Guards and Patrol Services at $307M and All Other Travel Arrangement and Reservation Services at $279M. SOUTHWEST VALLEY CONSTRUCTORS CO leads vendors at $283M, CSI AVIATION, INC follows at $278M, and WHITING-TURNER CONTRACTING COMPANY, THE follows at $155M."
      }
    ]
  },
