    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Homeland Security spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $2.1B on contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Homeland Security made 3,019 awards with an average award size of $704K, and obligations fell 97.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $20.8B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $23.6B in FY24, $28.3B in FY25, and $73.3B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Homeland Security buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security buys a mix of construction, services, and technology in FY2027 to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is $609M, Security Guards and Patrol Services is $307M, All Other Travel Arrangement and Reservation Services is $279M, Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation is $152M, and Computer Systems Design Services is $105M; other categories include Engineering Services at $103M and Ship Building and Repairing at $92.3M."
